# game/ch4_attack.rpy:19
translate plain ch4_attack_3f37004e:

    # narrator "Day 60. Something is wrong with the chain the way something can be wrong with a house at night — quietly, and in your own walls."
    narrator "Day 60. Something is wrong on the blockchain."
    narrator "It feels like a strange sound in your house at night. Quiet. And coming from inside your own walls."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:24
translate plain ch4_attack_9d57b965:

    # s "it's happening. tonight. you have maybe one move before it starts. use it."
    s "it's happening. tonight. you have time for maybe one move before it starts. use it."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} The multisig is your shared wallet that needs several people to approve payments. Hardening it and rotating means making it stricter and replacing every key with a new one."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Alerting the community means telling all members now, so many more people are watching."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:28
translate plain ch4_attack_8c1a72d1:

    # s "done. it won't stop them. it will slow them. sometimes that's the whole war."
    s "done. it won't stop them. it will slow them down."
    s "sometimes slowing them down is the whole fight."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:31
translate plain ch4_attack_07fe3d58:

    # s "loud. risky. but a thousand eyes see more than mine."
    s "loud. risky. but a thousand people can see more than i can alone."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:45
translate plain ch4a_phish_6d631dee:

    # narrator "1:14 a.m. A routine treasury payout is queued — vendor invoice, seen a hundred times. Your wallet extension summarizes it cheerfully."
    narrator "1:14 a.m. A normal treasury payment is waiting for your signature. It's a vendor invoice, the kind you've seen a hundred times."
    narrator "Your wallet extension shows you a short, cheerful summary of it."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:47
translate plain ch4a_phish_98f3be12:

    # narrator "Maya would have caught the smell of it. Maya is gone."
    narrator "Maya would have noticed something was wrong. But Maya is gone."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:50
translate plain ch4a_phish_f49652fc:

    # m "Something's off. My extension updated itself an hour ago and I didn't approve that."
    m "Something's wrong. My wallet extension updated itself an hour ago."
    m "I didn't approve that update."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:54
translate plain ch4a_phish_fdc93eb6:

    # narrator "SIGN TRANSACTION?\n\nTo: Vendor Payments Ltd [OK]\nAmount: 12.5 ETH [OK]\nGas: normal [OK]"
    narrator "SIGN TRANSACTION?\n\nTo: Vendor Payments Ltd [OK]\nAmount: 12.5 ETH [OK]\nGas: normal [OK]"

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:55
translate plain ch4a_phish_232cb2bd:

    # narrator "Everything looks fine. It is 1:14 a.m. Your Burnout is [burnout]. The confirm button is very large and very green."
    narrator "Everything looks fine. It is 1:14 a.m. Your Burnout is [burnout]."
    narrator "The confirm button is very big and very green."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} The summary is your wallet app's short, friendly version of the payment. The raw data is the real transaction code, written in hex: numbers 0–9 and letters a–f."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} An address is a long code for a wallet. The whitelist is your list of addresses you already trust."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:60
translate plain ch4a_phish_5646e145:

    # narrator "The 'summary' was drawn by malware. The real destination was 0x7C3f…a91E — a fresh wallet, already tumbling your 60 ETH into fog."
    narrator "The 'summary' was fake. Malware, bad software hidden on your computer, drew it."
    narrator "The real destination was 0x7C3f…a91E, a brand-new wallet. It is already mixing your 60 ETH through other wallets, so nobody can follow it."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:64
translate plain ch4a_phish_1190bb1e:

    # narrator "You expand the raw data. The hex swims — you're too tired for this.\n\nWhitelist: {color=#578C88}0x4A21…9DEB{/color}\nDestination: {color=#9D908D}0x4A2l…9DE8{/color}\n\n(Is that an l? An 8? You genuinely cannot tell tonight.)"
    narrator "You expand the raw data. The hex swims in front of your eyes. You're too tired for this.\n\nWhitelist: {color=#578C88}0x4A21…9DEB{/color}\nDestination: {color=#9D908D}0x4A2l…9DE8{/color}\n\n(Is that an l? An 8? You really cannot tell tonight.)"

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:66
translate plain ch4a_phish_aecb21f3:

    # narrator "You expand the raw data.\n\nWhitelist: {color=#578C88}0x4A21…9DEB{/color}\nDestination: {color=#D3710D}0x7C3f…a91E{/color}\n\nNot even close."
    narrator "You expand the raw data.\n\nWhitelist: {color=#578C88}0x4A21…9DEB{/color}\nDestination: {color=#D3710D}0x7C3f…a91E{/color}\n\nThey are not even close."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:71
translate plain ch4a_phish_ffd5a438:

    # narrator "Rejected. Somewhere, an attacker's script moves to plan B. The ugly little hardware screen just earned its keep."
    narrator "Rejected. Somewhere, the attacker's program switches to plan B."
    narrator "The ugly little hardware screen just proved it was worth having."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:76
translate plain ch4a_phish_57090a80:

    # narrator "It was not a display bug."
    narrator "The screen was not wrong."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:82
translate plain ch4a_phish_74354c50:

    # j "Three members say the site asked them for weird token approvals tonight. Probably nothing? The mint is LIVE, [player_name]."
    j "Three members say our site asked them for weird token approvals tonight. Probably nothing?"
    j "The mint is LIVE, [player_name]!"
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} A token approval lets an app move your tokens for you. The front end is the website members use."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Taking it down stops the mint while you investigate. Keeping it up lets the mint continue while the reports are unchecked."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:87
translate plain ch4a_phish_2987cf2f:

    # narrator "You pull the plug on your own party. Post-mortem: injected script, harvesting approvals — a stolen CDN key. Three wallets grazed. It would have been three hundred."
    narrator "You shut down your own party. The post-mortem finds the cause: someone stole your CDN key and injected a script into the site."
    narrator "It was phishing: the script was tricking people into token approvals. Three wallets lost a little. It would have been three hundred."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:92
translate plain ch4a_phish_467e0f33:

    # narrator "By morning, ninety wallets are drained — your believers' wallets, not the treasury. That's the one loss you can't refund."
    narrator "By morning, phishing has drained ninety wallets. These are your supporters' wallets, not the treasury."
    narrator "That is the one loss you cannot pay back."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:102
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_2f22caf7:

    # m "RED ALERT. One entity just crossed 45%% of governance tokens. Eleven wallets, one owner."
    m "RED ALERT. One owner just went over 45 percent of all governance tokens."
    m "Eleven wallets. One owner."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:104
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_625e7801:

    # narrator "The alert comes from a community dashboard, hours late — the person who would have watched it in real time doesn't work here anymore. One entity holds 45%%."
    narrator "The alert comes from a community dashboard, hours late. The person who would have watched it live doesn't work here anymore."
    narrator "One owner holds 45 percent."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:107
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_c90cf47d:

    # a "It's Atlas. I'd know that gas-price signature anywhere. You have maybe a day before the proposal drops. Use it."
    a "It's Atlas. I know how his wallets pay gas. It's like a fingerprint."
    a "You have maybe one day before his proposal goes up. Use it."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:109
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_ce83956e:

    # narrator "The proposal appears at dawn: 'Treasury Diversification Initiative.' Professional. Reasonable. Beautifully formatted."
    narrator "The proposal appears at dawn: 'Treasury Diversification Initiative.' The title means spreading the treasury money across different things."
    narrator "It looks professional. Reasonable. Beautifully formatted."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:111
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_ad586491:

    # narrator "Buried in the code: a drain to an address Atlas controls. Your time-locks force a 7-day review — which is why anyone found it at all."
    narrator "Hidden in the code is a drain: it sends money to an address Atlas controls."
    narrator "Your time-locks force a 7-day review before it can run. That's the only reason anyone found it."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:114
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_0668bf72:

    # narrator "Buried in the code: a drain function. And with no time-locks, it executes the moment it passes. A charming proposal to fund an animal shelter posts an hour later. (The distraction.)"
    narrator "Hidden in the code is a drain function, code that sends the money out. With no time-locks, it runs the moment the vote passes."
    narrator "An hour later, a charming proposal to fund an animal shelter appears. (It's a distraction.)"

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:117
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_59f1083b:

    # w "Nothing personal, founder. Someone responsible was always going to end up holding the keys. I'd hoped you'd hand them over gently."
    w "Nothing personal, founder."
    w "Someone responsible was always going to end up holding the keys. I had hoped you would hand them over gently."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} An emergency pause uses your founder key to freeze all governance at once. Only you can do it, so the DAO is less decentralized."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Community defense, if offered, means many small holders delegate together to outvote the whale. Negotiating means paying Atlas to leave."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:125
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_d6298007:

    # narrator "The attack stops. So does the pretense. 'Decentralized until it's inconvenient' — the quote-tweet does numbers. A splinter group forks off as 'TrueDAO' by the weekend."
    narrator "The attack stops. So does the pretending. People mock you: 'Decentralized until it's inconvenient.' The post spreads everywhere."
    narrator "By the weekend, a group splits away and forks the project as 'TrueDAO'."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:131
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_8e0f599c:

    # v "Solidarity is a governance primitive. Always was."
    v "Solidarity, people standing together, is one of the basic building blocks of governance."
    v "It always was."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:132
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_3621be96:

    # narrator "Twelve hundred small wallets delegate to trusted stewards overnight. The proposal fails, 52 against. Atlas's tokens sit there, suddenly just... money."
    narrator "Overnight, twelve hundred small wallets delegate to trusted stewards. The proposal fails, 52 against."
    narrator "Atlas's tokens are still there. But suddenly they are just... money. They have no power."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:137
translate plain ch4b_fiftyone_8f4e89e7:

    # w "One hundred ETH and I walk away. Consider it a governance tax. Cheaper than the lesson, which you are also receiving."
    w "One hundred ETH and I walk away. Consider it a governance tax: the price of weak defenses."
    w "It's cheaper than the lesson. Which, by the way, you are also getting."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:146
translate plain ch4c_spiral_649eb656:

    # narrator "No attacker this time. Just weather: the market drops 40%% in a week, and your token — being 90%% of your treasury — drops harder."
    narrator "No attacker this time. Just bad weather in the market."
    narrator "The market drops 40 percent in a week. Your token falls even harder, and it is 90 percent of your treasury."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:149
translate plain ch4c_spiral_4a245c0e:

    # m "Treasury purchasing power is down 70%%. Payroll is Thursday. I want it on record that I said the word 'barbell' in this room."
    m "Our treasury can buy 70 percent less than before. Payroll is Thursday."
    m "For the record: I said the word 'barbell' in this room. Keep a safe part in stables. Remember?"

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:150
translate plain ch4c_spiral_13f38153:

    # narrator "The spiral logic is simple and airless: you need cash » you sell your token » the price falls » you need more cash."
    narrator "The spiral logic is simple, and there's no air in it: you need cash » you sell your token » the price falls » you need more cash."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Selling native tokens gets cash for payroll now, but selling pushes the price lower. An emergency raise means taking Atlas's money without knowing his terms."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Hibernating means cutting spending and pausing pay, to survive as something small."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:157
translate plain ch4c_spiral_bd3aae32:

    # narrator "Payroll clears. The chart now looks like a ski slope, and the community watched you shove."
    narrator "Payroll is paid. But the price chart now goes down like a ski slope."
    narrator "And the community watched you push it down."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:164
translate plain ch4c_spiral_ee5f6338:

    # w "Of course. Happy to help. We can discuss governance... later."
    w "Of course. Happy to help."
    w "We can discuss governance... later."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:169
translate plain ch4c_spiral_dfb8f197:

    # narrator "Contributor pay paused. Grants paused. Dreams: paused. But the lights, technically, stay on."
    narrator "Contributor pay: paused. Grants: paused. Dreams: paused."
    narrator "But technically, the lights stay on. The project is still alive."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:178
translate plain ch4_triage_e296016c:

    # narrator "Casualty accounting, morning after: Treasury [treasury] ETH. Vibes [vibes]. Security [security]. Morale [morale]. Burnout [burnout] — crises bill the founder first."
    narrator "The next morning, you count the damage. Treasury [treasury] ETH. Vibes [vibes]. Security [security]. Morale [morale]. Burnout [burnout]."
    narrator "In every crisis, the founder pays first."

# game/ch4_attack.rpy:179
translate plain ch4_triage_1263d944:

    # narrator "The collective is still here. Changed — the way a house is changed by a fire it survived."
    narrator "The collective is still here. But it has changed."
    narrator "It's like a house that survived a fire. Still standing, but never quite the same."

